From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:27:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] fix(motion): one Outside-air check for every Outside Arc
 entry path

Safety review of #3899 (pullrequestreview-6043099439): a stand-in on an
Outside pass was still chosen inside the ladder, after the one plan-level
refusal. One rule closes the class: a selected Arc on an Outside ring pass
goes down in air outside the stock, or the op is refused by name
(OUTSIDE_AIR_REFUSAL, now in approach.rs and read by approach::refusal).

entry_warn::outside_air_check is the one check. It is called by:
- the plan (pocket.rs, pocket_avoid.rs), now also for an Adaptive op on
  its fallback to Offset rings;
- air_entry::stand_in, the first entry of a level with no air lead;
- entry_warn::outside_arc_restart, the re-entry after a lift (both
  descent_dive::entry_restart and descent_dive::restart).

Pins: outside_first_entry_without_an_air_lead_is_refused,
outside_reentry_without_an_air_lead_is_refused, and
outside_pocket_arc_without_air_is_refused over Waterline, Offset rings
and Adaptive. The clamp pin now accepts a move in air or the refusal.

Refs #3884

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
