From e95fb87e09a2e455c84110b639f18b4a4c4435ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:06:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] fix(motion): an Outside Arc re-entry may come down on cut
 floor

Coordinator decision C on #3899: outside_air_check also accepts the floor
that is already cut at that depth, as #3855 does. A re-entry after a lift
onto a pass start in material on an Outside pass with the Arc entry now
comes down in air outside the stock, or by a plunge whose tool disc is
all on the floor already cut at that depth (the lift point first, then
rings round the start), with a link at depth through cut floor that
crosses no earlier cut. Only a plunge into uncut stock is refused.

Pins: outside_reentry_onto_cut_floor_is_accepted,
outside_reentry_without_an_air_lead_is_refused.

Refs #3884

